## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where editing a configured hook transform could leave the gateway running the old transform function after hooks hot reload rebuilt the mapping config.

## Why This Change Was Made

Hook mapping resolution now drops the process-local transform function cache when hooks config is resolved, and transform cache misses import with one cache-bust token for the current reload generation so Node does not reuse the previous module instance. A delayed import from an older generation can still finish its own delivery, but it no longer republishes into the current cache after a reload.

## User Impact

Operators can update hook transform files and have subsequent matching webhook deliveries use the edited transform without restarting the gateway.

## Evidence

- Production module boundary: `pnpm exec tsx ../../outputs/local-hook-transform-reload/proof-live.ts`

```text
$ pnpm exec tsx ../../outputs/local-hook-transform-reload/proof-live.ts
first-transform: before
after-reload: after
```

- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/hooks-mapping.test.ts`: 30 passed, including an overlapping-import regression where an older delayed import finishes after reload without replacing the new-generation cache.

